.TH SKAN 1 "31 August 2026" "Skan" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skan \- first-party modular network scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skan
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B skan scan
.I target-spec
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B skan discover
.I ip-address
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B skan resolve
.I target-spec
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skan is a Linux-first C++20 network scanner supporting bounded target
resolution, host discovery, TCP and UDP scanning, service detection, OS
fingerprinting, and normal, JSON, XML, or grepable output.
.PP
Targets may be IPv4 or IPv6 addresses, CIDR ranges, inclusive address ranges,
hostnames, or comma-separated mixtures. Use only on systems and networks for
which you have authorization.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Display the Skan version.
.TP
.BR \-sT , " --method connect"
Use unprivileged TCP connect scanning.
.TP
.B \-sS
Use TCP SYN scanning. Live raw-packet operation requires root or explicitly
reviewed Linux capabilities.
.TP
.B \-sU
Use bounded UDP scanning. Live raw-packet operation may require root.
.TP
.B \-sn
Perform discovery only.
.TP
.B \-Pn
Skip host discovery.
.TP
.B \-sV
Enable service and version detection.
.TP
.B \-O
Enable OS fingerprinting.
.TP
.BR \-4 , " \-6"
Restrict resolved targets to IPv4 or IPv6.
.TP
.BI "\-p " port-spec
Select ports using a single port, comma-separated list, range, or
.B \-p\-
for all TCP ports.
.TP
.BI "--top-ports " count
Scan the selected number from Skan's deterministic common TCP port corpus.
.TP
.BI "--exclude " target-spec
Exclude resolved targets. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI "--exclude-ports " port-spec
Exclude ports from the active TCP or UDP selection.
.TP
.B --open
Display only open or open-or-filtered ports.
.TP
.B --reason
Display port-state reasons in normal output.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color in normal terminal output.
.TP
.B --debug
Enable diagnostic engine logging. Diagnostic output is disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "--service-db " path
Override the default service-probe database.
.TP
.BI "--os-db " path
Override the default OS-fingerprint database.
.TP
.BI "--output " format
Select normal, JSON, XML, or grepable output.
.TP
.BR \-oN , " \-oX , " \-oG
Write normal, XML, or grepable output to a file.
.TP
.BI "\-oA " prefix
Write normal, XML, and grepable output files using a shared prefix.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/skan/service-probes.db
Default service probe database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/skan/udp-probes.db
Default UDP probe database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/skan/os-fingerprints.db
Default IPv4 OS fingerprint database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/skan/os-fingerprints-v6.db
Default IPv6 OS fingerprint database.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The installed executable is not set-user-ID and receives no capabilities.
TCP connect scans normally run without root. Live SYN, UDP, and other
raw-packet modes can require
.BR sudo (8).
Skan reports capability failures and does not silently fall back.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
skan -sT -p 22,80,443 192.0.2.10
sudo skan -sS --top-ports 100 192.0.2.10
sudo skan -sU -p 53 192.0.2.10
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR capabilities (7),
.BR sudo (8)
